<edge_cases>
<edge_case id="TITLE_TRUNCATION">
  Script truncates titles to ~70 characters at word boundaries (no mid-word cuts):
  kebab_title truncated at last hyphen if length exceeds 70
</edge_case>
<edge_case id="SPECIAL_CHARACTERS">
  Script removes non-alphanumeric characters except spaces, then converts spaces to hyphens and collapses consecutive hyphens
</edge_case>
<edge_case id="EMPTY_TITLE">
  Script falls back to using just the task ID: task-<id_num>
</edge_case>
</edge_cases>

<thoughts_handling>
The `thoughts/` directory is excluded from automatic symlinking to prevent merge conflicts across worktrees.

<behavior>thoughts/ is skipped by default. The script never creates a symlink for this directory.</behavior>

<when_to_symlink>Only symlink `thoughts/` if it is tracked in `.gitignore`: CREATE_THOUGHTS_SYMLINK=true ~/.claude/scripts/create-worktree.sh --id=42</when_to_symlink>

<alternatives>
  1. Copy manually: cp -r /path/to/main/repo/thoughts .
  2. Add to .gitignore: echo "thoughts/" >> .gitignore
  3. Keep task-specific notes in the worktree, general notes in main repo
</alternatives>
</thoughts_handling>

